`PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK = False` **on the imported module object before calling
`_build_anchor_rows`**. I did not edit the pilot file. The call therefore traversed the
dormant branch beginning at `scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:544`, using setting `a-r0`,
carrier `nearest-eligible`, the shipped shortlist support, 100 users, the pilot's calibrated
values, and boundary indices `(0,)`. The source literal remains `True` on disk at line 89.

[RUN] Exact-path generation achieved 39 anchors across both requested worlds: 19 in
`V025_PROBE/world/1` and 20 in `V025_PROBE/world/2`, totaling 38,311 rows. The coherent
model snapshot contains 37 anchors (world 1 steps 0–17; world 2 steps 0–18), 36,360 rows,
3,700 `(anchor,user)` groups, and 160,444 non-tied true within-group pairs. Two further
anchors finished atomically while interrupt shutdown propagated; they are included in row
verification and timing but excluded from modeling because the sealed-fit cache had already
snapshotted the 37-anchor prefix.

[RUN] The requested 60 anchors were not reached. The exact-path timing over all 39 generated
anchors was:

| path | mean s/anchor | median | IQR | min–max |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| declared dormant branch | 474.75 | 401.64 | 380.37–434.95 | 343.27–1,721.77 |
