## Fit and metric definitions

[RUN] The sealed C1 fit used the repository's `AdamMLPHead` and literal values from
`src/mcrl/stagec_v025/learner.py:44-62`: hidden `(8,)`, ReLU, learning rate `1e-2`,
Adam `(0.9, 0.999)`, epsilon `1e-8`, zero weight decay, and `gauge_beta = 0.2`.
Every fold received exactly 2,000 source epochs and one deterministic full-batch update per
epoch. As in the shipped pilot, a deterministic `linspace` aggregate retained 4,096
base-to-candidate pairs (`scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:1149-1163`). LOAO used the first
sealed pilot learner seed (`V025_LEARNER/seed/1`, integer
`6407676579069309528`); LOWO reports the mean over all four sealed pilot seeds and retains
their ranges in the JSON.

[RUN] The plain linear reference minimized the same pairwise squared objective plus the
same `0.2` reference gauge in closed form on the same 4,096-pair fold aggregates. It was
not a scalar-label convenience regression.

[RUN] Metrics are pooled over held-out rows/groups:

- level `R²`: raw head scores against normalized targets, including exact-zero BASE rows;
  no test-time re-gauging;
- ordering: all non-tied true action pairs within each held-out `(anchor,user)` group;
  prediction ties receive `0.5`;
- top-1: stable predicted argmax counts as correct when its true target equals the group's
  maximum within `1e-12`.

## Required held-out comparisons

[RUN] Values below are the single fixed LOAO seed and the four-seed mean for LOWO where a
seeded head is involved. Full per-seed values and ranges are in
[`results.json`](/home/sat/mcrl-v025-c1c2-ws/.scratch/c1-declared/results.json).

| model / target | LOAO R² | LOAO order | LOAO top-1 | LOWO R² | LOWO order | LOWO top-1 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| sealed `(8,)`, declared | −0.2724 | 0.5889 | 0.1711 | −0.6507 | 0.5945 | 0.1863 |
| plain linear, declared | −0.1506 | 0.5715 | 0.0835 | −0.2451 | 0.5579 | 0.0922 |
| sealed `(8,)`, surrogate | −133,527.0572 | 0.6594 | 0.2254 | −21,454.4750 | 0.6179 | 0.2667 |
| `Φ`-only | −0.2073 | 0.4499 | 0.1749 | −0.2073 | 0.4499 | 0.1749 |
| constant (training-fold mean) | −0.0058 | 0.5000 | 0.1716 | −0.0005 | 0.5000 | 0.1716 |

[RUN] The declared sealed head beats constant ordering by `0.0889` but does not beat the
constant's level `R²` or top-1. The linear reference has better level `R²` than the sealed
head but worse ordering and much worse top-1. The `Φ`-only ranker is below chance ordering;
the physical surplus is not recoverable by preference alone.

### Surrogate contrast

[RUN] The surrogate is easier for ordering on the fixed LOAO seed (`0.6594` versus
`0.5889`) and top-1 (`0.2254` versus `0.1711`), but its raw level fit is not stable under
the sealed architecture. LOWO seed ranges were:

- `R²`: `−85,816.5571` to `0.4650` (median `−0.9040`);
- ordering: `0.4111` to `0.7393` (median `0.6607`);
- top-1: `0.0181` to `0.4770` (median `0.2858`).

[RUN] A direct rerun of the extreme LOAO lineage found true surrogate labels only in
`[−1.7023, 1.9676]`, while raw predictions ranged from `−2,248.66` to `1,127.34`.
The worst repeated non-reference rows had primitive Q1 slot 1
(`nominal_required_power_over_cap`) equal to `1,000,000` and target `0.0`. Thus the huge
negative `R²` is an actual out-of-range prediction caused by primitive-state extrapolation,
not a serialization error. The surrogate is “easy” only in the narrower ranking/selected-
seed sense; it is not a stable sealed-head level problem on this panel.

## Capacity versus information

[RUN] Widened heads changed only the hidden width; activation, optimizer, learning rate,
gauge, pair aggregate, epoch budget, and seeds stayed fixed.

| declared-target model | LOAO R² | LOAO order | LOAO top-1 | LOWO R² | LOWO order | LOWO top-1 |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| width 8 | −0.2724 | 0.5889 | 0.1711 | −0.6507 | 0.5945 | 0.1863 |
| width 32 | −0.3066 | 0.5980 | 0.1527 | −0.9040 | 0.5765 | 0.1987 |
| width 128 | −0.6840 | 0.5999 | 0.1995 | −2.5058 | 0.5537 | 0.1844 |
| high-capacity 16-256-256 nonlinear basis | **0.0933** | **0.6197** | 0.1854 | **−0.0714** | **0.5987** | 0.1941 |

[RUN] The high-capacity probe used fixed-seed two-layer ReLU random features, all raw slots,
and a 529-parameter ridge output. Ridge strength was selected inside every outer fold using
training-only anchor validation from `{0.01, 0.1, 1, 10, 100, 1000}`. It is much more
flexible than the linear reference and produced the best observed held-out `R²` of any
tested function of the 16 slots.

[INFERRED] There are two effects. First, sealed optimization/architecture hurts level fit:
`−0.2724` versus the flexible `0.0933`. Second, the flexible ceiling itself is low and does
not materially improve top-1; widening the sealed head makes level transfer worse. The
evidence therefore points primarily to missing information, with secondary architecture/
optimization harm. Because this is one high-capacity family on 37 anchors and two worlds,
“informational ceiling” means the best observed explanation, not a theorem about every
possible regressor.

## Which inputs carry the observed signal

[RUN] Permutation importance uses the high-capacity LOWO model. One slot was globally
permuted inside each held-out world fold; entries are drops from baseline LOWO
`R² = −0.07136`, ordering `0.59869`, and top-1 `0.19405`. Zero-based slots match the
repository schema in `src/mcrl/stagec_v025/state.py:29-46`.

| slot | feature | ΔR² | Δordering | Δtop-1 |
|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|
| 0 | nominal SINR margin | 0.2203 | 0.0362 | 0.0432 |
| 1 | required power / cap | 0.0000 | 0.0000 | 0.0000 |
| 2 | nominal spectral efficiency | 0.1601 | 0.0371 | 0.0627 |
| 3 | background occupancy | 0.0311 | 0.0191 | −0.0216 |
| 4 | beam active before focal | 0.0349 | 0.0232 | 0.0508 |
| 5 | satellite active before focal | 0.0678 | 0.0025 | 0.0257 |
| 6 | off-axis angle | 0.0000 | 0.0000 | 0.0000 |
| 7 | remaining D2 time | 0.1669 | 0.0492 | 0.0827 |
| 8 | remaining visibility time | 0.0670 | 0.0464 | 0.0592 |
| 9 | refresh phase | 0.1043 | 0.0178 | 0.0503 |
| 10 | previous served association | 0.0422 | 0.0127 | −0.0184 |
| 11 | previous served load | 0.0055 | 0.0003 | 0.0454 |
| 12 | previous beam active | 0.0491 | 0.0279 | 0.0851 |
| 13 | previous satellite active | 0.0822 | 0.0260 | 0.0265 |
| 14 | previous beam max RF / cap | 0.0578 | 0.1057 | 0.0778 |
| 15 | missing incumbent | 0.0000 | 0.0000 | 0.0000 |

[RUN] Slots 6 and 15 are exactly zero throughout the panel. Slot 4 equals
`1[slot 3 > 0]` with zero violations, and slot 12 equals `1[slot 11 > 0]` with zero
violations.

[DERIVED] The effective dimension is therefore `16 − 2 constant − 2 redundant = 12`.
Separate permutation attribution inside `(3,4)` and `(11,12)` is arbitrary: each member
can substitute for the other, and independent permutation creates combinations absent from
the real encoder. Pair-level importance, not the split between members, is the defensible
reading.

[INFERRED] The largest observed level carriers are current SINR margin, remaining D2 time,
spectral efficiency, and refresh phase. They provide some predictive signal but do not
encode the complete whole-network bits/energy response required by
`c1_difference_surplus`; the weak flexible held-out ceiling is consistent with that
compression.

